# Go
/backend/bin/
/backend/perspectivegraph
*.test
*.out
# Coverage ARTEFACTS only. This was `coverage.*`, which also matched Go SOURCE: adding
# internal/coverage/coverage.go silently committed its test without its implementation,
# and every Go job in CI failed to build. A pattern broad enough to swallow a .go file
# has no business in a Go repository.
coverage.html
coverage.txt
coverage.xml

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
/frontend/dist/
/frontend/.vite/
*.local
# single-use working notes (e.g. launch drafts)
*.local.md

# TypeScript composite build outputs (emitted by `tsc -b`)
*.tsbuildinfo
/frontend/vite.config.js
/frontend/vite.config.d.ts

# Env & secrets
.env
# Docker secret files (docker-compose.secrets.yml mounts these). Real credentials
# live here; nothing under it may ever be committed.
/secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
/tls/

# Editor / OS / local tooling
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.swp

# macOS/iCloud conflict copies: "name 2.go", "name 3.json". This directory is under
# ~/Documents, which iCloud Drive syncs, and a copy lands beside the original with the
# same content. One of these was committed and broke the build rather than a test: Go
# compiles "npmversion_test 2.go" as ORDINARY source - the name does not end in
# _test.go - so it landed in the package proper, where the helper it calls only exists
# in a test file. `go build ./...` failed, and so did the release image build.
* [0-9].*
* copy.*
* copy [0-9].*

# Data volumes (docker)
/.data/
node_modules.nosync/

# The gate writes its machine-readable verdict here when run with -json.
verdict.json
